    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWith ui2 enabled, 'cmdheight' 0 and the default message target, a message\nshown before `:s///c` leaves the confirm prompt invisible. The prompt still\nworks: typing `y` replaces the match.\n\nRelated: #18958 had the same symptom before ui2, and #40282 was another\nproblem with a cmdline message under ui2 and 'cmdheight' 0.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`repro.lua`:\n\n```lua\nvim.o.cmdheight = 0\nrequire('vim._core.ui2').enable({})\nvim.defer_fn(function()\n  vim.notify('3 items due')\nend, 200)\n```\n\n```sh\nprintf 'foo one\\nfoo two\\n' > sub.txt\nnvim --clean -u repro.lua sub.txt\n```\n\nWait a second, then type `:%s/foo/bar/gc<CR>`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe prompt `replace with bar? (y)es/(n)o/...` is visible. It is when any one\nof these holds:\n\n- 'cmdheight' is 1\n- ui2 is not enabled\n- no message was shown before the command\n- messages go to the msg window: `{ msg = { targets = { default = 'msg' } } }`\n  on nightly, or `{ msg = { target = 'msg' } }` on 0.12.5\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1738+g521eddec7c (nightly, 2026-09-27). Also NVIM v0.12.5.\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo; ui2 is Nvim only.\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 7.0.0-31-generic\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ntmux 3.7c, run detached (`tmux new-session -d`)\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nNightly: the nvim-linux-x86_64.tar.gz release asset. 0.12.5: conda-forge.\n",
