            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for checking. The prompt is only hidden if the message is still on screen when `:` is typed. A key press or click before that dismisses the message, and then the prompt shows. This repro types the command itself, so it needs no input:\n\n```lua\nvim.o.cmdheight = 0\nrequire('vim._core.ui2').enable({})\nvim.defer_fn(function()\n  vim.notify('hello')\nend, 200)\nvim.defer_fn(function()\n  vim.api.nvim_input(':%s/foo/bar/gc<CR>')\nend, 1000)\n```\n\nRun `nvim --clean -u repro.lua sub.txt` and wait. The last line shows `hello`, and the prompt is missing. Without the `vim.notify()` call, the prompt shows. I see this on 6512282c55 and 0.12.5, both in tmux and in Nvim's `:terminal`.\n\nThe analysis below is by Claude Opus 5.5.\n\nThe cause seems to be timing in ui2. When the `:s` cmdline closes, `cmdline_hide()` schedules closing the expanded cmd window ([cmdline.lua#L145-L152](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6512282c55651d21a64c9e43624b84f013cdde14/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/cmdline.lua#L145-L152)). That callback runs after the confirm prompt is drawn, and `check_targets()` reopens the window hidden because 'cmdheight' is 0 ([ui2.lua#L96](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6512282c55651d21a64c9e43624b84f013cdde14/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2.lua#L96)). While the prompt waits, the cmd buffer holds the prompt text, but its window has `hide = true`.\n",
            "created_at": "2026-09-28T09:35:50Z",
